<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Le Moyne d&apos;Iberville is a 43-year-old naval commander treated seven weeks ago with chloroquine and primaquine for relapsing P. vivax malaria, who comes for a preventive visit. He has had no fever, chills or sweats since the treatment and no dark urine. He carries his fever card. He is preparing a squadron that is expected to sail early next year for French Guiana and the French Antilles, and his pre-travel vaccines are planned for the summer visit. He walks the dockyard most days and sleeps about seven hours. He wants his prevention brought up to date before the deployment. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 43</td></tr><tr><td>Malaria</td><td>No fever since chloroquine and primaquine</td></tr><tr><td>Deployment</td><td>Expected to sail early next year</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>AUDIT-C 3</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Delacroix-Boateng. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good since the malaria treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Busy and under pressure preparing the squadron; supportive household</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Wine with dinner, about eight drinks a week; AUDIT-C 3</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks the dockyard most days; sails</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; fish and bread, few vegetables</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>No concerns; one partner</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Works on ladders and rigging in the dockyard; can swim</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hearing normal by his report; reads without glasses</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

