    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Tetanus, diphtheria and pertussis booster given; HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn; lipids normal for his age with no other risk factor; colorectal cancer screening begins at 45. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis B triple panel decides whether he needs hepatitis B vaccine before the deployment.</item><item>Travel vaccines at the pre-travel visit in the summer.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Relapsing P. vivax malaria, after radical cure (B51.9)</content>. No relapse five weeks after finishing primaquine. [S]<list><item>Continue the fever action plan.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol</content>. AUDIT-C 3, below the threshold for unhealthy use. [S]<list><item>Brief advice to stay within two drinks a day, and to take care with alcohol in the heat at sea.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>120/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 3; brief advice given</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>LDL cholesterol 116 mg/dL, HDL 52 mg/dL; no diabetes, smoking or hypertension; no statin indicated</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 22.6 with no other risk factor; glucose 92 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45; no family history recorded</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening and vaccination</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel drawn today; hepatitis B vaccine before the deployment if he is not immune</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap today; no dose recorded in the last ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Travel vaccines</td><td>Due</td><td>Yellow fever, hepatitis A and typhoid at the pre-travel visit, as the consultant advised</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>In the autumn, before the deployment</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sun protection at sea discussed; hat and sunscreen</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Treatment of Uncomplicated Malaria (clinical guidance) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Pre-travel vaccine visit in the summer. Screening results through the patient portal. Next scheduled visit 1705-07-28: pre-travel visit: yellow fever, hepatitis A, hepatitis B and typhoid vaccines, and the travel plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
